1
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:04,540
You're here.

2
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:07,380
Your organs are failing.

3
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:09,300
And your death is drawing near.

4
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:13,440
But if you bribe the right politicians in the right order at the right time,

5
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:16,600
you can trade the nuclear warheads for medicine.

6
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:20,080
And it's not even a crime.

7
00:01:39,984 --> 00:01:43,624
A one percent Treaty You have enough nuclear weapons to kill everyone thirteen

8
00:01:43,624 --> 00:01:44,404
times.

9
00:01:44,964 --> 00:01:49,304
Here's how to settle for twelve point eight seven times and use the savings

10
00:01:49,304 --> 00:01:49,984
on medicine.

11
00:01:50,784 --> 00:01:52,044
Controversial, apparently.

12
00:01:52,544 --> 00:01:56,604
The world spends two point seven two trillion dollars a year on military

13
00:01:56,604 --> 00:01:57,124
forces.

14
00:01:57,764 --> 00:02:02,524
If every nation reduces that by one percent at the same time, the balance

15
00:02:02,524 --> 00:02:04,424
of power remains identical.

16
00:02:05,064 --> 00:02:06,884
No country becomes more vulnerable.

17
00:02:07,244 --> 00:02:10,384
Nobody loses a single war they would have otherwise won.

18
00:02:10,844 --> 00:02:15,024
You just become slightly less capable of destroying a planet you're still

19
00:02:15,024 --> 00:02:15,744
living on.

20
00:02:16,324 --> 00:02:21,124
That one percent is twenty-seven point two billion dollars a year.

21
00:02:21,724 --> 00:02:25,744
For comparison, that's roughly what Americans spend on Valentine's Day.

22
00:02:26,284 --> 00:02:31,584
You are currently spending more on heart-shaped candy than on curing heart disease.

23
00:02:31,584 --> 00:02:36,784
A one percent treaty is a piece of paper that says every signatory nation

24
00:02:36,784 --> 00:02:42,064
redirects that one percent to enable any patient to participate in pragmatic

25
00:02:42,064 --> 00:02:45,303
clinical trials for the most promising new treatments.

26
00:02:45,864 --> 00:02:46,364
That's it.

27
00:02:46,724 --> 00:02:47,964
That's the whole idea.

28
00:02:48,644 --> 00:02:52,684
On Wishonia, we fought for twelve thousand years before we figured this

29
00:02:52,684 --> 00:02:53,184
out.

30
00:02:53,544 --> 00:02:57,804
Your species has been thinking it over for several thousand years, so you're

31
00:02:57,804 --> 00:02:59,124
actually ahead of schedule.

32
00:02:59,944 --> 00:03:00,904
How It Works.

33
00:03:00,904 --> 00:03:01,824
Funding.

34
00:03:02,584 --> 00:03:06,924
It creates a twenty-seven point two billion dollars a year revenue stream

35
00:03:06,924 --> 00:03:09,064
for the one percent Treaty Fund.

36
00:03:09,864 --> 00:03:10,364
Execution.

37
00:03:11,004 --> 00:03:16,264
A network of Decentralized Institutes of Health subsidizes patient participation

38
00:03:16,264 --> 00:03:18,844
in a decentralized F.D.A.,

39
00:03:19,524 --> 00:03:23,264
clinical trials that are forty-four point one times cheaper than the current

40
00:03:23,264 --> 00:03:23,764
model.

41
00:03:24,444 --> 00:03:24,964
Governance.

42
00:03:25,464 --> 00:03:31,044
Global population via Wishocracy, with transparent auditable rules and automated

43
00:03:31,044 --> 00:03:32,044
fund allocation.

44
00:03:33,304 --> 00:03:33,804
Transparency.

45
00:03:33,924 --> 00:03:37,684
All research, data, and spending published on a public ledger.

46
00:03:38,604 --> 00:03:40,584
This Isn't a Trade-Off.

47
00:03:40,584 --> 00:03:44,524
It's like if everyone in your neighborhood spent their life savings on attack

48
00:03:44,524 --> 00:03:49,683
dogs, and then called it a "safe community" because all the dogs are equally

49
00:03:49,683 --> 00:03:50,183
vicious.

50
00:03:50,824 --> 00:03:55,344
When every nation builds one percent fewer explosion devices at the same

51
00:03:55,344 --> 00:03:57,564
time, you get two good things:

52
00:03:58,064 --> 00:03:58,944
You become safer.

53
00:03:59,544 --> 00:04:04,024
The global "you might all die by accident" temperature drops one percent.

54
00:04:04,024 --> 00:04:07,944
Fewer chances of someone pressing the wrong button, which happens more than

55
00:04:07,944 --> 00:04:08,444
you'd think.

56
00:04:08,904 --> 00:04:11,204
You stop dying from stupid things.

57
00:04:11,684 --> 00:04:16,284
That twenty-seven point two billion dollars pays sick people to try treatments

58
00:04:16,284 --> 00:04:18,204
instead of waiting for death.

59
00:04:19,104 --> 00:04:24,184
Economists call this a Kaldor-Hicks improvement, which is their way of saying

60
00:04:24,184 --> 00:04:28,544
"the winners win more than the losers lose, and we've decided that counts."

61
00:04:29,244 --> 00:04:33,784
In practice, some weapons manufacturers lose one percent of their contracts.

62
00:04:34,284 --> 00:04:39,444
In exchange, they and everyone they love become less likely to die of cancer.

63
00:04:40,304 --> 00:04:42,664
Most people consider this a good trade.

64
00:04:43,584 --> 00:04:45,404
Defense contractors are still doing the math.

65
00:04:46,364 --> 00:04:51,244
Why Your Most Expensive Things Are Also Your Most Useless Things (A Mystery).

66
00:04:52,064 --> 00:04:56,664
When countries "invest" in military hardware, they're not buying assets.

67
00:04:57,084 --> 00:05:00,924
They're buying very expensive paperweights that occasionally explode.

68
00:05:01,684 --> 00:05:05,544
A bridge lets trucks drive over it every day, which creates something called

69
00:05:05,784 --> 00:05:09,844
"economic activity," which is when money moves around instead of sitting

70
00:05:09,844 --> 00:05:10,344
still.

71
00:05:10,964 --> 00:05:13,604
A bridge lasts fifty to one hundred years.

72
00:05:14,104 --> 00:05:15,264
It makes everyone richer.

73
00:05:15,644 --> 00:05:16,944
It's quite nice to look at.

74
00:05:16,944 --> 00:05:21,724
A missile also sits still, but instead of trucks driving over it, it just...

75
00:05:21,724 --> 00:05:22,224
waits.

76
00:05:22,484 --> 00:05:24,004
For the day it gets to be a missile.

77
00:05:24,624 --> 00:05:26,404
Most missiles never get that day.

78
00:05:26,844 --> 00:05:30,424
They just sit in a hole until someone throws them away, which costs more

79
00:05:30,424 --> 00:05:31,764
than buying them in the first place.

80
00:05:32,484 --> 00:05:35,864
It's like adopting a dog that you're never allowed to walk, and it costs

81
00:05:35,864 --> 00:05:39,924
one point five million dollars a year in food, and if it ever gets out it

82
00:05:39,924 --> 00:05:40,744
kills everyone.

83
00:05:41,564 --> 00:05:45,604
Economists call this "dead capital," which means resources trapped in a

84
00:05:45,604 --> 00:05:47,464
form that can't do anything useful.

85
00:05:48,104 --> 00:05:50,364
It's like converting your house into a pile of T.N.T.

86
00:05:51,464 --> 00:05:55,564
Impressive, but you can't live in it, rent it out, or do anything except

87
00:05:55,564 --> 00:05:59,943
eventually blow it up, at which point you have neither a house nor T.N.T.

88
00:06:01,044 --> 00:06:02,984
As President Eisenhower put it:

89
00:06:03,384 --> 00:06:08,584
"Every gun that is made, every warship launched, every rocket fired signifies,

90
00:06:08,584 --> 00:06:13,584
in the final sense, a theft from those who hunger and are not fed, those

91
00:06:13,584 --> 00:06:15,364
who are cold and are not clothed."

92
00:06:16,224 --> 00:06:20,264
Eisenhower was a five-star General, which means he had five stars.

93
00:06:20,784 --> 00:06:24,864
Most generals only get three or four, so he was basically the Michelin Guide

94
00:06:24,864 --> 00:06:25,884
of killing people.

95
00:06:26,384 --> 00:06:31,384
He personally ran the largest military operation in human history, the invasion

96
00:06:31,384 --> 00:06:32,124
of Normandy.

97
00:06:32,724 --> 00:06:35,284
And even he thought you were overdoing it.

98
00:06:36,124 --> 00:06:43,044
A one percent treaty doesn't ask you

99
00:06:43,044 --> 00:06:44,861
to spend twenty-seven point two billion dollars curing diseases.

100
00:06:44,861 --> 00:06:46,264
It asks you to redirect twenty-seven point two billion dollars from the

101
00:06:46,264 --> 00:06:50,184
least useful one percent of your military budget to things that make you

102
00:06:50,184 --> 00:06:51,504
richer and less dead.

103
00:06:52,524 --> 00:06:53,124
The Blueprint.

104
00:06:54,404 --> 00:06:57,284
A treaty is basically a promise between countries.

105
00:06:57,664 --> 00:07:00,824
Like a pinky swear, but with more lawyers and fewer pinkies.

106
00:07:01,384 --> 00:07:05,104
The thing about promises between countries is that nobody can actually make

107
00:07:05,104 --> 00:07:08,564
them keep the promise, because the only people who could punish a country

108
00:07:08,564 --> 00:07:11,904
are other countries, and they're all busy breaking their own promises.

109
00:07:11,904 --> 00:07:15,764
Sometimes treaties work (you haven't had World War Three yet).

110
00:07:16,544 --> 00:07:19,684
Sometimes they don't (you've had about two hundred other wars).

111
00:07:20,224 --> 00:07:23,424
But they're the only tool you have for getting countries to do anything

112
00:07:23,424 --> 00:07:25,364
together besides kill each other.

113
00:07:26,544 --> 00:07:27,544
What Each Country Pays.

114
00:07:28,804 --> 00:07:32,604
Every signatory nation contributes exactly one percent of their military

115
00:07:32,604 --> 00:07:34,924
budget to the one percent Treaty Fund.

116
00:07:34,924 --> 00:07:39,484
U.S.A., eight point eight six billion dollars, which sounds like a lot until

117
00:07:39,484 --> 00:07:43,584
you learn they once lost two point four six trillion dollars in accounting

118
00:07:43,584 --> 00:07:44,624
errors at the Pentagon.

119
00:07:45,244 --> 00:07:45,824
Not spent.

120
00:07:46,484 --> 00:07:48,844
*Lost.* As in, they don't know where it went.

121
00:07:48,844 --> 00:07:53,764
Two point four six trillion dollars just wandered off, like a cat.

122
00:07:54,224 --> 00:07:56,324
And unlike a cat, nobody put up posters.

123
00:07:57,164 --> 00:08:01,744
China, two point nine six billion dollars (what they spend on military parades).

124
00:08:01,744 --> 00:08:06,844
India, eight hundred and thirty-five million dollars (one aircraft carrier's

125
00:08:06,844 --> 00:08:07,464
wine budget).

126
00:08:08,424 --> 00:08:12,084
Russia, one point zero nine billion dollars (Putin's shirt budget).

127
00:08:12,764 --> 00:08:16,884
Saudi Arabia, seven hundred and fifty-four million dollars (one prince's

128
00:08:16,884 --> 00:08:17,384
yacht).

129
00:08:17,904 --> 00:08:22,804
U.K., six hundred and eighty-six million dollars (the National Health Service,

130
00:08:22,984 --> 00:08:27,544
or N.H.S., waiting list is currently longer than some of the wars this money

131
00:08:27,544 --> 00:08:28,384
is meant to prevent).

132
00:08:29,044 --> 00:08:32,684
France, five hundred and sixty-three million dollars, which is what they

133
00:08:32,684 --> 00:08:33,744
spend on...

134
00:08:33,744 --> 00:08:37,164
well, it's France, so probably something involving cheese or being disappointed

135
00:08:37,164 --> 00:08:37,984
in other countries.

136
00:08:38,744 --> 00:08:42,144
The French military has a long and proud history of things I'm not going

137
00:08:42,144 --> 00:08:44,144
to get into because this is a book about medicine.

138
00:08:45,044 --> 00:08:45,904
And so on...

139
00:08:46,724 --> 00:08:50,004
National Security (Which Is What You Call It When You Spend Money on Things

140
00:08:50,004 --> 00:08:51,124
That Don't Make You Secure).

141
00:08:52,084 --> 00:08:54,024
What actually threatens nations today:

142
00:08:54,664 --> 00:08:56,804
Real Threats (That Actually Kill People).

143
00:08:56,804 --> 00:08:58,284
One.

144
00:08:58,284 --> 00:08:58,784
Pandemics:

145
00:08:59,304 --> 00:09:03,804
COVID killed more Americans than World War Two, Korea, and Vietnam combined.

146
00:09:04,144 --> 00:09:07,524
But you don't have a Department of Pandemics with an eight hundred and eighty-six

147
00:09:07,524 --> 00:09:09,444
billion dollar budget and a flag.

148
00:09:09,444 --> 00:09:10,139
Two.

149
00:09:10,139 --> 00:09:10,834
Cancer:

150
00:09:10,834 --> 00:09:15,544
Kills ten million people a year, which is more than the population of Sweden.

151
00:09:16,584 --> 00:09:20,304
Essentially, Sweden is being completely eliminated by cancer every twelve

152
00:09:20,304 --> 00:09:22,584
months and nobody's declared war on it.

153
00:09:22,984 --> 00:09:25,224
Well, Nixon did, in nineteen seventy-one.

154
00:09:25,224 --> 00:09:26,464
Cancer won.

155
00:09:26,464 --> 00:09:27,083
Three.

156
00:09:27,083 --> 00:09:28,324
Heart Disease:

157
00:09:28,324 --> 00:09:30,404
eighteen million annual deaths.

158
00:09:30,924 --> 00:09:35,064
You are, as mentioned, spending more on heart-shaped candy than on this.

159
00:09:35,064 --> 00:09:36,644
Four.

160
00:09:36,644 --> 00:09:37,144
Dementia:

161
00:09:37,404 --> 00:09:39,684
Destroying the minds of every nation's elderly

162
00:09:40,364 --> 00:09:44,024
(and sometimes their leaders, which you'd think would speed things up, but no).

163
00:09:44,024 --> 00:09:45,864
Five.

164
00:09:45,864 --> 00:09:46,364
Climate Disasters:

165
00:09:46,644 --> 00:09:49,054
Making entire regions uninhabitable.

166
00:09:49,054 --> 00:09:50,144
Six.

167
00:09:50,144 --> 00:09:51,124
Mental Health Crisis:

168
00:09:51,704 --> 00:09:53,984
More people kill themselves than die in wars.

169
00:09:54,524 --> 00:09:55,924
The wars have a dedicated budget.

170
00:09:56,284 --> 00:09:57,524
The suicides do not.

171
00:09:58,324 --> 00:10:01,284
Overfunded Threats (That Countries Spend Trillions On).

172
00:10:01,864 --> 00:10:02,924
Other Countries Attacking:

173
00:10:03,504 --> 00:10:04,044
It happens.

174
00:10:04,384 --> 00:10:04,884
It's real.

175
00:10:05,144 --> 00:10:05,664
Ask Ukraine.

176
00:10:06,304 --> 00:10:11,164
But disease kills two hundred and twenty-five times more people every year,

177
00:10:11,484 --> 00:10:13,564
and you're funding them in the opposite ratio.

178
00:10:14,744 --> 00:10:15,283
Terrorists:

179
00:10:15,283 --> 00:10:18,344
Kill fewer people than furniture accidents.

180
00:10:18,684 --> 00:10:21,264
But here's the part your defense budget doesn't advertise:

181
00:10:22,384 --> 00:10:26,244
military occupation is the primary *cause* of terrorism.

182
00:10:27,424 --> 00:10:32,064
Robert Pape at the University of Chicago analyzed every suicide terrorist

183
00:10:32,064 --> 00:10:36,284
attack from nineteen eighty to two thousand and three and found that ninety-five

184
00:10:36,284 --> 00:10:42,104
percent were responses to foreign military occupation, not religious ideology.

185
00:10:42,884 --> 00:10:46,604
The group that committed the most suicide attacks during that period was

186
00:10:46,604 --> 00:10:48,344
the Tamil Tigers of Sri Lanka:

187
00:10:49,104 --> 00:10:52,044
Marxist atheists who invented the suicide vest.

188
00:10:52,524 --> 00:10:53,644
Not a mosque in sight.

189
00:10:54,544 --> 00:10:59,124
Half of all suicide attackers in the dataset had no religious motivation

190
00:10:59,124 --> 00:10:59,804
whatsoever.

191
00:11:00,764 --> 00:11:06,844
Your eight trillion dollar War on Terror killed nine hundred thousand people

192
00:11:06,844 --> 00:11:12,344
and global terrorist attacks went from about one thousand per year to nearly

193
00:11:12,344 --> 00:11:16,424
seventeen thousand per year by twenty fourteen.

194
00:11:16,424 --> 00:11:20,644
Nearly all of them targeted democracies that had stationed military forces

195
00:11:20,644 --> 00:11:22,004
in the attackers' homeland.

196
00:11:22,804 --> 00:11:28,084
You spent eight trillion dollars making the problem seventeen times worse.

197
00:11:28,824 --> 00:11:31,584
Your military bases aren't protecting you from terrorism.

198
00:11:32,044 --> 00:11:34,164
They're the reason it's pointed at you.

199
00:11:34,164 --> 00:11:37,684
A one percent treaty addresses the real threats.

200
00:11:38,064 --> 00:11:41,264
It doesn't weaken your ability to handle the conventional ones.

201
00:11:41,804 --> 00:11:44,284
You keep ninety-nine percent of your weapons.

202
00:11:44,744 --> 00:11:48,614
If ninety-nine percent of your military can't handle the job, the last one

203
00:11:48,614 --> 00:11:50,204
percent wasn't going to save you.

204
00:11:50,784 --> 00:11:53,364
Besides, you've done far bigger cuts before.

205
00:11:53,884 --> 00:11:56,084
After World War Two, the U.S.

206
00:11:56,084 --> 00:12:00,384
slashed military spending by eighty-seven point six percent in two years

207
00:12:00,724 --> 00:12:05,784
(from one point four two trillion dollars to one hundred and seventy-six

208
00:12:05,784 --> 00:12:07,824
billion dollars in today's dollars). G.M. went from building Cadillacs to building B twenty-four bombers, won the war, and went back to Cadillacs. Frigidaire stopped making machine guns and returned to refrigerators. Nobody held a congressional hearing about whether the refrigerator industry could survive without the machine gun contracts. Frigidaire just made refrigerators again. It wasn't complicated. It was only complicated later, when the machine gun industry hired lobbyists. The economy didn't collapse. It produced the greatest boom in your history. Today you're spending thirty point six times the pre-World War Two baseline in inflation-adjusted dollars: twenty-nine billion dollars in nineteen thirty-nine versus eight hundred

209
00:12:07,824 --> 00:12:11,124
and eighty-six billion dollars today, during peacetime, with no existential

210
00:12:11,124 --> 00:12:12,684
threat requiring it.

211
00:12:13,304 --> 00:12:17,984
Your defense industry learned how to make peacetime feel like wartime (see

212
00:12:17,984 --> 00:12:19,244
Regulatory Capture).

213
00:12:19,824 --> 00:12:23,184
You're asking to redirect one percent of that.

214
00:12:24,424 --> 00:12:25,684
The Rebranding Campaign:

215
00:12:25,684 --> 00:12:28,744
From "Weakness" to "Strategic Genius".

216
00:12:29,744 --> 00:12:31,364
Politicians hate looking weak.

217
00:12:31,584 --> 00:12:35,004
It's their biggest fear, right after having to use their own healthcare

218
00:12:35,004 --> 00:12:35,504
system.

219
00:12:36,064 --> 00:12:39,204
So you don't frame this as "reducing military spending."

220
00:12:39,664 --> 00:12:40,724
You frame it as:

221
00:12:40,724 --> 00:12:43,604
"The Strategic Health Defense Initiative".

222
00:12:44,164 --> 00:12:48,924
The old frame ("We're cutting defense by one percent") is political suicide.

223
00:12:49,424 --> 00:12:53,764
The new frame ("We're building a biodefense shield against the real threats")

224
00:12:54,004 --> 00:12:55,284
is political genius.

225
00:12:56,124 --> 00:12:56,824
Same policy.

226
00:12:56,824 --> 00:12:58,204
Different adjective.

227
00:12:58,924 --> 00:13:01,724
Your species can be manipulated with adjectives.

228
00:13:02,164 --> 00:13:06,744
This is simultaneously the most depressing and most useful fact about you.

229
00:13:07,464 --> 00:13:10,324
The Talking Points That Make Hawks Sound Like Doves.

230
00:13:11,004 --> 00:13:11,664
For Conservatives:

231
00:13:12,144 --> 00:13:15,984
"This protects American lives from diseases, which are basically immigrants

232
00:13:15,984 --> 00:13:17,444
that got past the immune system.

233
00:13:17,944 --> 00:13:21,264
It's the Strategic Defense Initiative for the twenty-first century, except

234
00:13:21,264 --> 00:13:21,764
it works.".

235
00:13:22,444 --> 00:13:23,064
For Liberals:

236
00:13:23,604 --> 00:13:26,544
"We're redirecting the tools of war to the cause of healing.

237
00:13:26,924 --> 00:13:29,924
This is how we build a more just and equitable world.".

238
00:13:30,744 --> 00:13:31,444
For Nationalists:

239
00:13:32,284 --> 00:13:35,684
"Our nation grows stronger when our people stop dying of diseases we can

240
00:13:35,684 --> 00:13:36,184
prevent.

241
00:13:36,464 --> 00:13:39,204
A healthy population is a powerful population.".

242
00:13:40,004 --> 00:13:40,704
For Economists:

243
00:13:41,424 --> 00:13:42,144
"The R.O.I.

244
00:13:42,144 --> 00:13:46,424
on the one billion dollar campaign to pass it is eighty-four point eight

245
00:13:46,424 --> 00:13:47,644
million to one.

246
00:13:47,964 --> 00:13:51,484
On paper, that beats every public health intervention on record.".

247
00:13:51,484 --> 00:13:53,584
For Conspiracy Theorists:

248
00:13:54,304 --> 00:13:58,064
"Big Pharma hates this one weird trick that makes medicine basically free.".

249
00:13:58,864 --> 00:13:59,624
For Everyone:

250
00:14:00,304 --> 00:14:01,284
"Your mom has cancer.

251
00:14:01,724 --> 00:14:02,864
This might cure it.

252
00:14:03,224 --> 00:14:03,764
Sign here.".

253
00:14:05,084 --> 00:14:05,664
The Money Flow.

254
00:14:06,624 --> 00:14:08,228
The one percent Treaty Fund.

255
00:14:08,228 --> 00:14:12,864
Twenty-seven point two billion dollars annually from military budgets flows

256
00:14:12,864 --> 00:14:14,664
into the one percent Treaty Fund.

257
00:14:15,144 --> 00:14:20,084
An eighty ten ten automatic split divides it before any funds reach discretionary

258
00:14:20,084 --> 00:14:20,664
spending:

259
00:14:20,664 --> 00:14:25,484
Eighty percent, or twenty-one point eight billion dollars, is allocated

260
00:14:25,484 --> 00:14:28,984
to Pragmatic Clinical Trials for patient subsidies, R.

261
00:14:28,984 --> 00:14:30,444
and D., and pandemic prep.

262
00:14:30,444 --> 00:14:35,944
Ten percent, totaling two point seven two billion dollars, goes to VICTORY

263
00:14:35,944 --> 00:14:39,904
Incentive Alignment Bond Returns for perpetual investor payments.

264
00:14:39,904 --> 00:14:45,324
Ten percent, also two point seven two billion dollars, is designated for

265
00:14:45,324 --> 00:14:49,744
Incentive Alignment Bond Political Incentives as rewards for supporting

266
00:14:49,744 --> 00:14:50,264
legislators.

267
00:14:51,264 --> 00:14:52,144
Notice what this does:

268
00:14:52,724 --> 00:14:54,904
it disentangles money from influence.

269
00:14:55,404 --> 00:14:58,344
In current government budgets, the people who provide the money

270
00:14:59,184 --> 00:15:01,964
(lobbyists, donors) also control where it goes.

271
00:15:02,544 --> 00:15:06,644
Money buys influence, influence redirects money, and the loop is invisible.

272
00:15:07,364 --> 00:15:10,144
Here, investors get money (ten percent).

273
00:15:10,144 --> 00:15:13,384
Politicians get career incentives (ten percent).

274
00:15:13,384 --> 00:15:17,344
Neither group touches the eighty percent that goes to clinical trials.

275
00:15:17,684 --> 00:15:21,744
The corruption is capped, transparent, and separated from the public goods

276
00:15:21,744 --> 00:15:22,244
funding.

277
00:15:23,244 --> 00:15:27,144
The eighty percent for pragmatic clinical trials is insulated from investor

278
00:15:27,144 --> 00:15:28,304
and political capture.

279
00:15:29,224 --> 00:15:33,504
Patients direct trial-participation spending by joining studies, while Wishocracy

280
00:15:33,504 --> 00:15:38,204
governs infrastructure and other shared medical public goods, not by a committee

281
00:15:38,204 --> 00:15:42,464
of twelve people in a conference room who haven't had a new idea since nineteen

282
00:15:42,464 --> 00:15:43,264
eighty-seven.

283
00:15:43,264 --> 00:15:47,704
Every human still gets direct say on the part that actually requires collective

284
00:15:47,704 --> 00:15:48,204
choice.

285
00:15:48,684 --> 00:15:50,244
Yes, even Florida Man.

286
00:15:51,384 --> 00:15:52,924
Year One Projected Outcomes.

287
00:15:53,704 --> 00:15:58,124
Only one point nine million participate in drug trials annually out of two

288
00:15:58,124 --> 00:16:00,724
point four billion people with chronic disease.

289
00:16:01,144 --> 00:16:04,224
With a one percent treaty plus a decentralized F.D.A.:

290
00:16:04,964 --> 00:16:08,798
Cost per patient is forty-one thousand dollars currently, but nine hundred

291
00:16:08,798 --> 00:16:13,284
and twenty-nine dollars with the treaty, making it forty-four point one

292
00:16:13,284 --> 00:16:14,124
times cheaper.

293
00:16:14,124 --> 00:16:19,344
Government trial funding is currently four point five billion dollars, with

294
00:16:19,344 --> 00:16:22,964
an additional twenty-one point eight billion dollars from the treaty.

295
00:16:23,704 --> 00:16:27,884
There are one point nine million patients per year currently, which would

296
00:16:27,884 --> 00:16:32,337
increase to twenty-three point four million under the treaty, a twelve point

297
00:16:32,337 --> 00:16:33,724
three times increase.

298
00:16:34,504 --> 00:16:35,684
The Incentive Structure.

299
00:16:36,304 --> 00:16:40,944
The military-industrial complex gets to keep ninety-nine percent of their

300
00:16:40,944 --> 00:16:46,164
budget (still plenty for bombs), pivot one percent to biotech (the health

301
00:16:46,164 --> 00:16:47,024
market is growing;

302
00:16:47,364 --> 00:16:49,684
the bomb market just got one percent smaller),

303
00:16:50,284 --> 00:16:51,064
look like heroes

304
00:16:51,704 --> 00:16:52,704
(rare for arms dealers),

305
00:16:53,324 --> 00:16:54,444
invest in the fund

306
00:16:55,364 --> 00:16:59,204
(VICTORY Incentive Alignment Bonds pay two hundred and seventy-two percent

307
00:16:59,204 --> 00:16:59,844
annually),

308
00:17:00,464 --> 00:17:02,264
and not die of cancer (even arms dealers get cancer).

309
00:17:02,944 --> 00:17:05,424
Especially the not dying of cancer part.

310
00:17:05,844 --> 00:17:06,504
The C.E.O.

311
00:17:06,504 --> 00:17:09,624
of Lockheed Martin has the same cells you do.

312
00:17:09,624 --> 00:17:12,704
Those cells malfunction on the same schedule.

313
00:17:13,284 --> 00:17:16,424
No amount of missile production has ever cured a tumor.

314
00:17:17,564 --> 00:17:18,784
Lockheed Martin Presents:

315
00:17:18,784 --> 00:17:21,084
The F thirty-five Cancer Killer.

316
00:17:21,784 --> 00:17:23,404
Boeing Proud Sponsor of:

317
00:17:23,404 --> 00:17:25,604
Not Dying of Alzheimer's.

318
00:17:25,964 --> 00:17:26,984
Raytheon Technologies:

319
00:17:27,544 --> 00:17:29,344
Now With one percent Less Death.

320
00:17:29,984 --> 00:17:31,244
They keep their contracts.

321
00:17:31,604 --> 00:17:32,564
They keep their profits.

322
00:17:32,944 --> 00:17:37,284
They just point one percent of their death machines at actual death.

323
00:17:37,284 --> 00:17:40,324
What Happens If This Actually Works.

324
00:17:41,104 --> 00:17:41,884
The Endgame.

325
00:17:42,524 --> 00:17:44,924
A one percent treaty isn't the goal.

326
00:17:45,184 --> 00:17:46,504
It's the proof of concept.

327
00:17:47,064 --> 00:17:51,264
I've watched roughly eight hundred and forty-seven civilizations reach this

328
00:17:51,264 --> 00:17:52,744
exact fork in the road;

329
00:17:53,124 --> 00:17:57,624
the ones still around all started with something like one percent, and the

330
00:17:57,624 --> 00:18:00,544
ones that didn't are geological features now.

331
00:18:01,164 --> 00:18:05,564
Once your species gets a taste of "spending money on things that help instead

332
00:18:05,564 --> 00:18:08,104
of things that explode," you'll want more.

333
00:18:08,864 --> 00:18:09,764
The Ratchet Effect.

334
00:18:09,764 --> 00:18:11,784
Public sentiment helps:

335
00:18:12,244 --> 00:18:14,624
once cures start rolling out, people want more.

336
00:18:15,124 --> 00:18:17,204
"Grandma's dementia is manageable now.

337
00:18:17,504 --> 00:18:19,464
Want to try another half-percent?"

338
00:18:19,464 --> 00:18:23,744
But your species has wanted cures for centuries without funding them.

339
00:18:24,644 --> 00:18:26,504
Popular demand alone doesn't move budgets.

340
00:18:27,204 --> 00:18:27,744
Money does.

341
00:18:28,464 --> 00:18:31,084
That's what the Incentive Alignment Bonds are for.

342
00:18:31,084 --> 00:18:35,824
Bondholders receive ten percent of all treaty inflows, perpetually.

343
00:18:36,464 --> 00:18:40,704
At one percent, that's two point seven two billion dollars a year split

344
00:18:40,704 --> 00:18:41,264
among them.

345
00:18:41,584 --> 00:18:45,063
At five percent, it's thirteen point six billion dollars.

346
00:18:45,063 --> 00:18:50,244
At full redirection, two hundred and seventy-two billion dollars.

347
00:18:50,244 --> 00:18:54,444
Every percentage point increase is a direct raise for every bondholder.

348
00:18:54,964 --> 00:18:56,404
These aren't random investors.

349
00:18:56,404 --> 00:19:01,424
They're billionaires, family offices, and institutional funds, people who

350
00:19:01,424 --> 00:19:06,083
already have senators on speed dial, media access, and campaign donation

351
00:19:06,083 --> 00:19:06,583
budgets.

352
00:19:07,103 --> 00:19:09,644
They didn't buy influence over the treaty fund.

353
00:19:09,984 --> 00:19:11,524
They bought a revenue share.

354
00:19:12,024 --> 00:19:16,164
But their pre-existing influence over everything else means any politician

355
00:19:16,164 --> 00:19:20,424
who tries to shrink or stall the treaty is picking a fight with the richest,

356
00:19:20,724 --> 00:19:25,204
most politically connected humans on the planet, all of whom have a quarterly

357
00:19:25,204 --> 00:19:29,824
earnings statement explaining why the treaty should be bigger, not smaller.

358
00:19:30,404 --> 00:19:34,544
The defense lobby built a permanent machine to keep military budgets growing.

359
00:19:34,544 --> 00:19:39,364
Incentive-alignment bonds, or I.A.B.s, build the mirror image:

360
00:19:39,704 --> 00:19:44,204
a permanent class of wealthy investors whose income scales directly with

361
00:19:44,204 --> 00:19:45,124
treaty expansion.

362
00:19:45,984 --> 00:19:50,664
Perpetual bonds mean a perpetual financial incentive to lobby for expansion,

363
00:19:50,664 --> 00:19:52,664
every single year, forever.

364
00:19:53,384 --> 00:19:58,044
Except these lobbyists have better math and a more popular product ("not

365
00:19:58,044 --> 00:19:59,384
dying" polls well).

366
00:20:00,024 --> 00:20:02,504
And the politicians on the receiving end of that pressure?

367
00:20:02,864 --> 00:20:04,244
They have their own math.

368
00:20:04,604 --> 00:20:09,284
The treaty's ten percent political incentive allocation scales with treaty

369
00:20:09,284 --> 00:20:09,784
size.

370
00:20:10,204 --> 00:20:15,004
At one percent, that's two point seven two billion dollars a year funding

371
00:20:15,004 --> 00:20:19,724
campaign support and post-office career rewards for legislators who voted yes.

372
00:20:19,724 --> 00:20:22,864
At five percent, it's five times that.

373
00:20:23,324 --> 00:20:28,044
A politician who votes to expand the treaty is voting to expand their own

374
00:20:28,044 --> 00:20:30,444
campaign war chest and retirement options.

375
00:20:31,104 --> 00:20:34,884
A politician who votes against expansion is voting to shrink them.

376
00:20:35,564 --> 00:20:38,984
Your species designed a system where politicians follow the money.

377
00:20:39,384 --> 00:20:41,804
This just points the money somewhere useful.

378
00:20:42,704 --> 00:20:45,164
More cures lead to more popular support.

379
00:20:45,644 --> 00:20:48,924
More bondholder income leads to more political pressure.

380
00:20:48,924 --> 00:20:53,844
More treaty funding leads to more campaign support for yes-voting politicians.

381
00:20:54,664 --> 00:20:56,264
Three ratchets, one direction.

382
00:20:56,984 --> 00:20:57,484
The endgame:

383
00:20:58,384 --> 00:21:02,584
countries bragging about their cancer survival rates instead of their missile

384
00:21:02,584 --> 00:21:03,084
counts.

385
00:21:03,804 --> 00:21:08,104
For quantitative projections of health and economic impacts, see impact

386
00:21:08,104 --> 00:21:10,344
dot war on disease dot O.R.G.

387
00:21:11,524 --> 00:21:13,764
Avoiding Treaty Pitfalls.

388
00:21:13,764 --> 00:21:15,704
Treaties fail in predictable ways.

389
00:21:15,704 --> 00:21:18,604
They all fail for the same boring reasons.

390
00:21:19,264 --> 00:21:22,044
Here's how this one avoids the common killers:

391
00:21:23,144 --> 00:21:23,864
Reservation Games.

392
00:21:24,864 --> 00:21:28,384
Countries love to sign treaties then add exceptions that gut them.

393
00:21:28,804 --> 00:21:31,744
It's like joining a gym but reserving the right to never go.

394
00:21:32,464 --> 00:21:32,964
Solution:

395
00:21:33,244 --> 00:21:34,564
No reservations permitted.

396
00:21:35,004 --> 00:21:35,584
All or nothing.

397
00:21:36,084 --> 00:21:36,944
Take it or leave it.

398
00:21:37,704 --> 00:21:38,644
Ratification Delays.

399
00:21:39,564 --> 00:21:43,044
Sign with fanfare, take a photo, then let it die in committee forever.

400
00:21:43,624 --> 00:21:45,624
Your species calls this "diplomacy."

401
00:21:45,624 --> 00:21:47,744
Solution:

402
00:21:47,744 --> 00:21:48,644
Provisional application.

403
00:21:48,644 --> 00:21:50,704
Takes effect on signature.

404
00:21:51,124 --> 00:21:53,884
Ratification just formalizes what already started.

405
00:21:54,744 --> 00:21:55,744
Creative Accounting.

406
00:21:55,744 --> 00:22:00,784
Reclassify "military" spending as "peacekeeping" or "homeland security"

407
00:22:00,784 --> 00:22:02,284
to dodge obligations.

408
00:22:02,884 --> 00:22:04,264
This is beige crime:

409
00:22:04,584 --> 00:22:08,284
making theft so procedurally dull that nobody investigates.

410
00:22:08,984 --> 00:22:13,544
Reclassifying "military" as "peacekeeping" is the bureaucratic equivalent

411
00:22:13,544 --> 00:22:18,644
of stealing someone's car by renaming it "shared mobility infrastructure."

412
00:22:19,924 --> 00:22:20,424
Solution:

413
00:22:20,604 --> 00:22:24,144
I.A.B.s make creative accounting self-defeating.

414
00:22:24,144 --> 00:22:28,424
Politicians who benefit from treaty compliance have personal financial incentive

415
00:22:28,424 --> 00:22:33,104
to ensure their nation's full one percent contribution flows through.

416
00:22:33,984 --> 00:22:38,684
Reclassifying military spending to dodge obligations reduces I.A.B.

417
00:22:38,684 --> 00:22:43,904
returns for that nation's own legislators, the same people who control budget

418
00:22:43,904 --> 00:22:44,804
classifications.

419
00:22:45,664 --> 00:22:46,884
Parliamentary Obstacles.

420
00:22:47,444 --> 00:22:50,704
Executive signs, legislature refuses to implement.

421
00:22:50,704 --> 00:22:51,224
Solution:

422
00:22:51,224 --> 00:22:53,084
The treaty obligates the percentage;

423
00:22:53,604 --> 00:22:58,864
Congress implements via the annual National Defense Authorization Act (N.D.A.A.).

424
00:22:59,624 --> 00:23:03,844
After Medellin versus Texas (two thousand and eight), the Supreme Court

425
00:23:03,844 --> 00:23:08,724
made clear that not all treaties are self-executing, so the treaty doesn't

426
00:23:08,724 --> 00:23:10,224
try to bypass Congress.

427
00:23:10,684 --> 00:23:15,464
It creates a binding international obligation that Congress fulfills through

428
00:23:15,464 --> 00:23:19,604
its normal appropriations process, the same way NATO's spending commitments

429
00:23:19,604 --> 00:23:20,104
work.

430
00:23:20,504 --> 00:23:23,824
The Incentive Alignment Bonds, or I.A.B.,

431
00:23:24,604 --> 00:23:29,404
mechanism ensures legislators have a personal incentive to include the one

432
00:23:29,404 --> 00:23:31,364
percent line item every year.

433
00:23:32,284 --> 00:23:32,784
Summary.

434
00:23:33,304 --> 00:23:35,924
A one percent treaty is a piece of paper that says

435
00:23:36,604 --> 00:23:41,524
"Let's spend one percent less on killing and one percent more on not dying.".

436
00:23:41,984 --> 00:23:42,484
That's it.

437
00:23:42,784 --> 00:23:43,504
That's the whole thing.

438
00:23:44,024 --> 00:23:45,284
It doesn't end war.

439
00:23:45,584 --> 00:23:47,184
It doesn't destroy the military.

440
00:23:47,624 --> 00:23:49,104
It doesn't create world peace.

441
00:23:49,504 --> 00:23:54,244
It just moves the *first* one percent of your murder budget to your survival

442
00:23:54,244 --> 00:23:54,744
budget.

443
00:23:55,304 --> 00:23:59,724
If you can't agree on that, if you can't agree that spending one penny less

444
00:23:59,724 --> 00:24:05,524
on death and one penny more on life is a good idea, then you deserve whatever's

445
00:24:05,524 --> 00:24:06,024
coming.

446
00:24:06,864 --> 00:24:07,364
Addendum:

447
00:24:07,944 --> 00:24:10,444
The Actual Treaty Text (First Draft).

448
00:24:11,124 --> 00:24:16,344
THE TREATY FOR THE ONE PERCENT REALLOCATION OF MILITARY EXPENDITURES TOWARDS

449
00:24:16,344 --> 00:24:20,924
BIOMEDICAL RESEARCH AND DEVELOPMENT FOR THE PREVENTION OF HUMAN SUFFERING

450
00:24:20,924 --> 00:24:22,384
AND DEATH (Or:

451
00:24:22,384 --> 00:24:25,004
The "Let's Not Die" Treaty, for short)

452
00:24:25,704 --> 00:24:31,924
WHEREAS, humanity spends two point seven two trillion dollars annually on

453
00:24:31,924 --> 00:24:33,604
methods of killing itself;

454
00:24:34,284 --> 00:24:37,084
WHEREAS, this seems somewhat counterproductive;

455
00:24:38,164 --> 00:24:43,524
WHEREAS, diseases kill more people than all wars combined and don't even

456
00:24:43,524 --> 00:24:45,564
have the decency to be quick about it;

457
00:24:45,564 --> 00:24:51,344
WHEREAS, we have nuclear weapons sufficient to end civilization thirteen

458
00:24:51,344 --> 00:24:54,584
times but haven't cured Alzheimer's once;

459
00:24:55,564 --> 00:24:56,064
WHEREAS,

460
00:24:56,544 --> 00:24:57,524
this is embarrassing;

461
00:24:58,564 --> 00:24:59,064
NOW,

462
00:24:59,624 --> 00:25:04,264
THEREFORE, the undersigned nations agree to try a different approach, as

463
00:25:04,264 --> 00:25:04,764
follows:

464
00:25:05,784 --> 00:25:07,024
Article One:

465
00:25:07,024 --> 00:25:12,044
Each signatory shall redirect exactly one percent of its annual military

466
00:25:12,044 --> 00:25:17,124
budget to the one percent Treaty Fund for allocation to pragmatic clinical

467
00:25:17,124 --> 00:25:17,864
trials.

468
00:25:18,964 --> 00:25:20,064
Article Two:

469
00:25:20,064 --> 00:25:23,464
Transfers shall be automatic, immediate, and irrevocable.

470
00:25:23,804 --> 00:25:25,384
No "we'll get to it later.".

471
00:25:26,444 --> 00:25:28,064
Article Three:

472
00:25:28,064 --> 00:25:30,924
Percentages may increase but never decrease.

473
00:25:31,384 --> 00:25:34,244
This is a ratchet, not a yo-yo.

474
00:25:34,244 --> 00:25:36,324
Article Four:

475
00:25:36,324 --> 00:25:39,864
Compliance shall be verified by public ledger and independent audits.

476
00:25:40,484 --> 00:25:41,704
No creative accounting.

477
00:25:41,704 --> 00:25:44,044
Article Five:

478
00:25:44,044 --> 00:25:47,324
Non-compliant parties lose access to I.A.B.

479
00:25:47,324 --> 00:25:49,644
benefits and treaty fund advantages.

480
00:25:50,184 --> 00:25:52,284
Your opponents get what you forfeit.

481
00:25:53,664 --> 00:25:55,184
Article Six:

482
00:25:55,184 --> 00:25:57,904
Success metrics trigger mandatory percentage reviews.

483
00:25:58,464 --> 00:26:00,084
When it works, we do more.

484
00:26:01,364 --> 00:26:02,804
Article Seven:

485
00:26:02,804 --> 00:26:05,864
Citizens have standing to enforce via domestic courts.

486
00:26:06,444 --> 00:26:09,070
You can sue your own government for non-compliance.

487
00:26:09,070 --> 00:26:10,964
Article Eight:

488
00:26:10,964 --> 00:26:16,404
Withdrawal requires unanimous consent of all parties plus ten-year notice.

489
00:26:16,984 --> 00:26:17,944
Good luck with that.

490
00:26:18,864 --> 00:26:19,844
Article Nine:

491
00:26:19,844 --> 00:26:23,464
This treaty supersedes all conflicting domestic law.

492
00:26:24,164 --> 00:26:25,944
Yes, even that law.

493
00:26:26,844 --> 00:26:28,424
Article Ten:

494
00:26:28,424 --> 00:26:30,944
Entry into force upon signature by two states.

495
00:26:31,444 --> 00:26:34,664
You only need two countries brave enough to go first.

496
00:26:35,024 --> 00:26:39,984
IN WITNESS WHEREOF, the undersigned, being of sound mind (debatable) and

497
00:26:39,984 --> 00:26:44,584
tired of watching their loved ones die of preventable diseases, have executed

498
00:26:44,584 --> 00:26:49,304
this Treaty on behalf of populations who would have executed it much sooner

499
00:26:49,304 --> 00:26:50,804
if anyone had asked them.

500
00:26:51,364 --> 00:26:55,944
Signed this day, blank, in the year of our ongoing confusion.

501
00:26:56,724 --> 00:26:57,264
Nation Name.

502
00:26:57,904 --> 00:26:59,724
"We choose life, I guess".

503
00:26:59,724 --> 00:27:00,404
P.S.

504
00:27:00,404 --> 00:27:03,204
- Yes, this includes space weapons.

505
00:27:03,204 --> 00:27:04,184
Nice try.

506
00:27:04,644 --> 00:27:05,264
P.P.S.

507
00:27:05,264 --> 00:27:07,304
- "Cyber weapons" too.

508
00:27:07,304 --> 00:27:08,424
